fact WorkItem(id: "WI-723", description: some(value: "Typer: a Relation named-tuple schema (r.T) does not resolve as a ROW-LAMBDA BINDER type — blocks WI-714 where/join. A row lambda c -> eq(c.x, v) passed to an op whose param projects the receiver schema (where(r, cond: (c: r.T) -> Bool)) needs the binder c typed at the CONCRETE schema so c.x (WI-638 named-tuple field access) type-checks. Diagnosed empirically in the WI-714 where increment: (a) a PREFIX call where(r, lam) does not resolve r.T at all — c stays at the abstract r.T; a DOT call r.where(lam) (receiver resolves the projection, like xs.find(lam)) is required. (b) even via dot-call, r.T resolves for a SCALAR (1-collapse Int64) schema but NOT for a NAMED-TUPLE (multi-column) schema — it stays abstract, so c.x fails: type mismatch in unresolved-receiver.x, no such member (dot dispatch). Acceptance: person_row.where(lambda c -> eq(c.name, x)) with person_row : Relation[(name: String, age: Int64)] type-checks with c : (name, age) and c.name : String. Likely a WI-638 / path-dependent-schema gap in lambda-binder context-typing. Rust typer only."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-15T19:18:52Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-723", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED (pending commit). ROOT CAUSE was mis-diagnosed: named-tuple schema elimination ALWAYS worked (a let-local receiver 'let pr = person_row; pr.where(l)' typed c:(name,age) correctly all along). The real bug: a bare RULE-reference receiver 'person_row.where(l)' MISLOWERED to a qualified name 'person_row.where' applied to the lambda (never a dot-call), because the WI-443 method-call re-route only fired for local/param heads. So where's arrow param (c: r.T)->Bool never hinted the lambda -> c stayed a fresh var -> c.name = <unresolved receiver>. The ticket's 'scalar resolves, named-tuple does not' was a SYMPTOM of the same mislowering (scalar eq(c,30) survives via unification; named-tuple c.name needs the type up front). FIX (2 edits, general, no where-special-casing): (A) load.rs try_identifier_dot_call: .or_else(resolve_qualified_rule_readonly(head)) so a rule head re-routes to a DotApply on the Relation sort; (B) typing.rs varref_arg_env_type: fall back to arg.inferred_type() so the pre-typed dot-call receiver's schema eliminates the callback projection (a rule ref is not in the value env). Tests wi723_row_lambda_binder_test.rs (4): named-tuple binder types + c.name concrete String + c.age concrete Int64 (negatives) + let-local parity. Full workspace green 2871/0. /code-review high (2 finders+verify): no correctness/soundness bug; watch-items F1 (WI-714 surface, recorded there) + F5 (theoretical false-reject, prevented by env-first+fresh-stamp).", at: "2026-07-15T19:08:23Z")
